--print-directory prints the directory, and then runs "git config --get remote.origin.url" to print
the origin URL, even for a clone that is not a git clone.  The goal file records the current
(wrong) behavior:  for a Mercurial clone, the program should not run git.  (Without --dry-run, the
git command fails silently in a Mercurial clone, unless the clone is inside a git clone.  If git is
not installed, the program exits with status 2, because it cannot run git.)
